1. Definitions

"Corresponding Source" means the preferred form for making modifications,
including all project-authored source code, interface definitions,
documentation, and scripts needed to build and package the Software or a
Derivative Work. It does not include third-party software available under its
own license from a public source identified in the distributed notices.

"Derivative Work" means a work based on or incorporating any material portion
of the Software, including a modified version or fork.

"Distribute" means to provide a copy of the Software or a Derivative Work to
another person or entity, whether in source, object, executable, or any other
form.

"Monetize" means to exercise rights in the Software or a Derivative Work to
provide a product or service to a third party for a fee or other consideration
when the product's or service's value derives entirely or substantially from
the Software. Monetization includes paid distribution, sale, rental,
subscription access, paid application listings, in-app purchases,
advertising-supported distribution, sponsorship-gated access, and paid
hosting, support, or consulting whose value derives substantially from the
Software. Charging no more than the documented cost of physical media and
delivery is not Monetization.

"Noncommercial Purpose" means a purpose that does not Monetize the Software or
a Derivative Work. Internal use by a person or organization, including a
business, is a Noncommercial Purpose when no third party is charged for access
to or value substantially derived from the Software.

